\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Low in the grave He lay,
\par Jesus, my Saviour;
\par Waiting the coming day,
\par Jesus, my Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Up from the grave He arose,
\par With a mighty triumph o'er His foes;
\par He arose a Victor from the dark domain,
\par And he lives for ever with His saints to reign:
\par He arose! Hallelujah! Christ arose!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Vainly they watch His bed,
\par Jesus, my Saviour;
\par Vainly they seal the dead,
\par Jesus, my Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Up from the grave He arose,
\par With a mighty triumph o'er His foes;
\par He arose a Victor from the dark domain,
\par And he lives for ever with His saints to reign:
\par He arose! Hallelujah! Christ arose!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Jesus, cannot keep his prey,
\par Jesus, my Saviour;
\par He tore the bars away,
\par Jesus, my Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Chorus\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Up from the grave He arose,
\par With a mighty triumph o'er His foes;
\par He arose a Victor from the dark domain,
\par And he lives for ever with His saints to reign:
\par He arose! Hallelujah! Christ arose!
\par \f1 
